WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.520
<b>New Monster
Proposal</b>

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:01.480
<b>New Monster</b>

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:01.480
<b>Proposal</b>

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:01.480
<b>Rejected</b>

00:00:00.910 --> 00:00:03.890
<i>When the cry of a newly-born 
monster rings out</i>

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.240
<i>from a secret society 
plotting world domination,</i>

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.940
<i>it sows destruction and 
chaos throughout the world,</i>

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:14.660
<i>and the madness this inspires 
creates monsters anew.</i>

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:17.540
<i>This is the tale of those who find allure 
in these incarnations of terror—</i>

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:20.370
<i>the Monster Development Department.</i>

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.270
<i>As long as good exists in this world,</i>

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:59.760
<b>Narrator</b>

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:59.760
<b>Masaru Shishido</b>

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:56.760
<i>so, too, shall evil thrive.</i>

00:01:57.610 --> 00:02:00.220
<i>But behind this eternal 
clash of good and evil,</i>

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.160
<i>there is another battle that goes unseen.</i>

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:06.770
Potential for aqueous combat?

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:12.020
<b>Secret Society: Agastia Monster Development Department
Assistant: Touka Kuroitsu</b>

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:12.020
<b>Secret Society Agastia Monster Development Department
New Assistant: Wolf Bete</b>

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:12.020
<b>Secret Society: Agastia Monster Development Department
{}Doctor: Hajime Sadamaki</b>

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:12.190
Yes. I thought it might be an avenue to 
explore in the fight against Blader.

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:14.320
I'm not so sure.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:17.700
I don't think you can even 
use a sword underwater.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:22.530
But wouldn't that mean Blader takes a big blow 
to his attack power if we drag him underwater?

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:24.840
True, but...

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:31.780
At the moment, we've only created monsters 
capable of going underwater, like Sahuagin.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:31.040
<b>Aquatic Monster
Sahuagin
(has gallstones)</b>

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:36.740
If we create a monster capable of fighting 
underwater, it might give us a big advantage.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:42.200
But the question is, how do 
we drag Blader underwater?

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.370
I overheard everything, 
Development Department!

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:47.990
Underwater monster combat...

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:49.940
<b>Secret Society: Agastia Great Leader
Akashic</b>

00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:49.380
An intriguing idea!

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:51.320
Lady Akashic!

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:54.720
One must always pursue new possibilities.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:56.530
I will allow it!

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.860
Now, let us proceed...

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:00.360
To the beach!

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:03.080
The beach?!

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:06.990
<b>— Episode 9 —

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:12.480
Miss Kuroitsu...

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:16.010
If this is just about testing monsters' 
underwater combat capability,

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:19.210
couldn't we have used the 
testing pool in the lab?

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:21.010
Well, sure,

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:24.320
but maybe she wants us to 
gather more real-world data.

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:26.370
Look, look! Kuroitsu!

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:28.490
It's a beachside food stand!

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:30.520
<b>Takoyaki</b>

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:30.520
<b>Hot Dogs</b>

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:30.520
<b>Yakisoba</b>

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:33.770
<b>Grilled Corn</b>

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:33.770
<b>Snow Cones</b>

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:33.770
<b>Ice Cream</b>

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:30.420
Let's buy some yakisoba!

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:33.770
<b>Yakisoba</b>

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:33.780
Never mind, she just wants to have fun.

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:39.260
It's a lot harder to work my 
devices without my AR goggles.

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:42.440
You're way too dependent 
on those things, Doctor.

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:43.650
Um...

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:47.660
<b>Long-Range Attack Specialized Monster
Cannon Thunderbird</b>

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:47.660
<b>Re-Regenerated • Regenerating Monster
New • Hydra</b>

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:47.660
<b>Chocolate Monster
Melty</b>

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:46.960
We kind of got dragged along 
without any explanation...

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:49.670
Can we ask why we're here?

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:53.000
Nominally, we're testing your 
compatibility with water.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:56.180
But you can probably just enjoy yourselves.

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:58.870
This is my first time at the beach.

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:00.920
What should I do?

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:03.410
A-Actually... Mr. Cannon...

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:07.010
This is... my first time at the beach, too.

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:10.930
Do you think we might spend it together?

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:12.190
Miss Hydra...

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:15.200
If you like, but...

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.930
The beach! The beach is calling me!

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:20.850
This is absurd. I'll burn to a crisp out here!

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:23.060
Make sure to apply plenty of sunscreen!

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:24.890
The ocean's full of sharks!

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:26.690
Bring it on, you toothy assholes!

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:29.630
Wonder if we'll see any sea slugs...

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:33.340
Hanging out with your sisters 
just seems really exhausting.

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:32.100
Bring it on!

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:33.710
Remember, you can get sunburn from 
the glare off the ocean, too.

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:33.710
Sea slugs! Sea slugs!

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:37.170
Cannon's so lucky...

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:39.570
He doesn't need to wear a swimsuit.

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:41.640
What's wrong, Wolfie boy?

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.200
Still not used to it?

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:44.730
Why the hell would I be?!

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:47.960
Dressing all girly-like 
is embarrassing as it is!

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:53.510
I wish you'd start embracing 
your feminine side already.

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:55.480
Where did that come from?!

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:57.740
Well, after all...

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:01.050
You're so adorable.

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:09.350
I guess that was a little overstimulating.

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:12.530
Miss Kuroitsu is so aggressive!

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:16.000
I can't hold out. I'm melting...

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:18.520
Miss Melty! Are you all right?

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:22.020
<i>The chocolate from which Melty 
was made required refrigeration.</i>

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:20.380
<b>Requires Refrigeration</b>

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:20.880
<b>Requires Refrigeration</b>

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:21.380
<b>Requires Refrigeration</b>

00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:24.310
C'mon, over here.

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:29.100
Lady Camula! Lady Arachne!

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.840
Thank you so much for coming.

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:31.570
Indeed.

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:34.420
I was surprised enough that 
Lady Camula wanted to come,

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:37.140
but I never dreamed you would 
join her, Lady Arachne.

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:40.650
<b>Pluripotent Cellular Executive
Immortal Camula</b>

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:40.650
<b>Dimension Shifting Executive
Weaver Monster Arachne</b>

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:41.280
Executives are required to undergo regular 
evaluations of their capabilities,

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:45.090
but she's always found excuses to skip out.

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:49.080
I figured this was the time to 
test how far she could swim.

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:50.720
The sun is too hot.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:53.390
The outside scares me.

00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:56.220
Hold my hand forever, Camula!

00:05:56.220 --> 00:05:58.670
Yeah, yeah. I hear you.

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:04.410
<i>I've heard that Lady Arachne's combat ability 
triples while she's inside her own castle.</i>

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:07.570
I'd love to learn your real specs!

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:11.430
Leave me alone! Let me 
go back to my territory!

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:14.860
We might actually be able to 
get some good data here.

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:15.440
I can't do it! I can't take any more!

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:19.410
Yay!

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:25.230
Looks like Matsu's not great at swimming.

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:30.040
If Matsu can't swim, maybe we can take over!

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:32.440
We're not a water snake 
monster for nothing!

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:36.390
I hadn't considered that the auxiliary 
heads might have swimming capabilities,

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:38.700
but they really are surprisingly versatile!

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:43.090
I didn't know the ocean was so salty!

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:45.770
Wanna cleanse your palate 
with a little lick of me?

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:48.670
Are you all better now?

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:50.340
Just fine, now that I'm cooled off!

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:53.360
And how are they doing?

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:54.920
Caught ya off-guard!

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:56.990
How d'you like that?

00:06:56.990 --> 00:06:59.900
A capabilities test is a contest of skill!

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:03.310
Let your guard down because it's a game,
 and you'll really feel the hurt!

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:05.850
I could say the same to you...

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:08.220
Senpai!

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:13.210
Not bad...

00:07:14.630 --> 00:07:16.470
You can't beat me at swimming!

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:20.720
I was second-best in my 
class at monster school!

00:07:20.990 --> 00:07:22.430
Did that really happen?

00:07:22.430 --> 00:07:24.750
In his mind, it did.

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:30.010
Monsters are given invented virtual reality 
memories when we're growing them.

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:47.510
What's with that "boy, 
I'm exhausted" expression?!

00:07:47.510 --> 00:07:50.990
You obviously had mechanical help!

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:53.730
Well, the mechanical bits 
are a part of me, too!

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:56.840
Cannon's body requires 
a lot of energy to run,

00:07:56.840 --> 00:07:59.940
but he can also channel that energy 
into a lot of different mechanisms.

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:02.470
And I guess they work in water, too.

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:04.510
He's doing pretty good, huh?

00:08:05.030 --> 00:08:06.060
This...

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:07.880
This battle isn't over yet!

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:10.180
Fine by me!

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:12.420
How shall we compete next?

00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:16.410
Hey, Arachne...

00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:21.780
Don't you think this is beneath 
the dignity of an executive?

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:31.740
All right, Wolfie boy!

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:32.410
Begin!

00:08:35.170 --> 00:08:36.660
Gotcha!

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:38.070
2.25 seconds!

00:08:38.070 --> 00:08:40.170
That's very impressive!

00:08:40.510 --> 00:08:44.680
Watermelon-smashing is no 
problem with a nose like mine!

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:52.530
3D mapping based on electromagnetic 
reflection, complete.

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:55.170
All right, Cannon! Begin!

00:08:57.280 --> 00:08:58.850
0.89 seconds!

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:01.740
Cannon... you...

00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:03.090
What's wrong, Senpai?

00:09:03.090 --> 00:09:04.990
It ain't like I'm cheatin'.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:10.160
What is it, Miss Hydra?

00:09:11.830 --> 00:09:14.690
Read the room, girly-boy!

00:09:14.690 --> 00:09:17.720
You're being way too suggestive with him!

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:19.880
Have a little sympathy for Matsu's 
complicated mental state!

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:21.170
You little...

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:21.930
What's with you guys?!

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:23.920
Quit pullin' on my swimsuit!

00:09:26.910 --> 00:09:30.630
The building of territory is the 
most beautiful thing in the world.

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:33.900
Venturing outside only brings danger.

00:09:34.530 --> 00:09:38.490
Yeah, I guess it's my own fault 
for bringing you here.

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:49.270
In combat above water, Cannon's long-range 
weapons give him an advantage.

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:54.180
Mr. Wolf might be stronger in the 
water where guns don't work as well.

00:09:54.350 --> 00:09:58.870
Why are they suddenly at each 
other's throats like this?

00:09:58.870 --> 00:10:01.310
You're so dense, Doctor.

00:10:01.940 --> 00:10:06.080
It's clearly because they both have 
someone they want to impress.

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:08.090
You think that's it?

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:20.500
I think I've thoroughly proven 
my superiority in the w—

00:10:27.510 --> 00:10:29.830
M-My body...

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:33.630
What's wrong, Cannon?!

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:38.020
I think something in my internal 
mechanisms shorted out.

00:10:38.690 --> 00:10:41.290
I can't move a muscle!

00:10:49.110 --> 00:10:51.640
Senpai! It's no use!

00:10:51.640 --> 00:10:53.800
I'm too heavy for you to lift!

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:57.540
But if you get totally flooded, 
you might end up out for good!

00:10:57.540 --> 00:10:58.800
But...

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:02.050
You think I'd leave you behind?
 We're a damn team!

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:06.760
Senpai...

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:10.130
Cannon!

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:11.420
Mr. Cannon!

00:11:18.770 --> 00:11:23.840
<i>Miss Hydra... Miss Melty... Miss Kuroitsu...</i>

00:11:24.230 --> 00:11:25.830
One, two...

00:11:28.210 --> 00:11:30.390
<i>I'm so worthless.</i>

00:11:30.390 --> 00:11:34.580
<i>After all my braggadocio, I end up like this.</i>

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:38.590
<i>And yet... Senpai still says we're a team.</i>

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:42.160
<i>Senpai... I'm sorry!</i>

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:44.480
Cannon, give me your location!

00:11:45.310 --> 00:11:46.560
That voice...

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:48.480
Great Leader!

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:52.270
<i>If I can just...</i>

00:11:56.220 --> 00:11:57.990
Hey, there he is!

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:00.740
One, two...

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:36.020
<b>Absolute Zero Chief of Staff
Megistus</b>

00:12:39.020 --> 00:12:44.530
<b>The Prophet Was a Little Girl?!</b>

00:12:39.930 --> 00:12:41.420
Great Leader,

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:44.530
<b>The
Second
Coming
of
Moses?!</b>

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:44.520
I realize that I approved this...

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:44.530
<b>Miracle at the Beach!</b>

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:48.960
But I believe I told you to be 
as inconspicuous as possible.

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:51.020
Sorry!

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:54.500
LONG-RANGE ATTACK SPECIALIZED MONSTER

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:54.500
