I</b>

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:44.940
There's a pub in a place like this?

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:51.060
<b>MISORI</b>

00:13:53.120 --> 00:13:54.480
Welcome!

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:55.550
Seating for one?

00:13:55.550 --> 00:13:56.490
Yes.

00:13:57.020 --> 00:13:58.500
Are you all right with the counter?

00:13:58.500 --> 00:13:59.820
That's just fine.

00:14:08.150 --> 00:14:09.570
Here's a menu.

00:14:09.860 --> 00:14:11.290
I'll start with a draft beer.

00:14:11.730 --> 00:14:13.330
One draft.

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:15.110
One draft coming up!

00:14:17.100 --> 00:14:19.090
What should I get?

00:14:19.090 --> 00:14:21.600
We recommend the amberjack today.

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:24.330
Oh, and we're out of curry and anpan.

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:27.330
<i>Curry and anpan at a pub?</i>

00:14:36.110 --> 00:14:39.540
<i>Beer just tastes special 
after a long day at work!</i>

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:42.450
<i>The business trip went great, 
and the food here is delicious!</i>

00:14:42.450 --> 00:14:44.330
<i>I'm putting today in the win column!</i>

00:14:48.730 --> 00:14:50.180
Mama, you got one?

00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:51.760
I'm out of my own...

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:54.930
I do have your special brand, Hachi.

00:14:56.520 --> 00:14:57.340
Here.

00:14:57.690 --> 00:14:59.560
Thanks, there's the ones.

00:15:21.500 --> 00:15:22.830
<i>That smell...</i>

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:25.830
<i>Polarized ozone generated 
by ionizing hafnium?</i>

00:15:25.830 --> 00:15:30.370
<i>That shouldn't be possible 
without a plasma control rod.</i>

00:15:31.020 --> 00:15:32.120
<i>Can it be...</i>

00:15:32.120 --> 00:15:35.530
<i>It's camouflaged, but it's 
nuclear reactor coolant!</i>

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:39.080
Talking about the past always 
gets me a little overheated.

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:41.410
Maybe I'll cool off outside.

00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:42.740
Come back soon.

00:15:43.190 --> 00:15:44.580
<i>I'm sure of it.</i>

00:15:44.580 --> 00:15:48.550
<i>That man has a miniature 
nuclear reactor in his body!</i>

00:15:48.820 --> 00:15:51.850
<i>Which means... he's a combat android?!</i>

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:54.990
It's past the statute of 
limitations now. So long ago...

00:15:55.560 --> 00:15:59.030
The day I was first assigned 
here, I got into a collision.

00:15:59.580 --> 00:16:03.390
It was a glancing blow, 
but the other guy died.

00:16:03.390 --> 00:16:05.560
That's awful.

00:16:05.780 --> 00:16:07.610
He happened to be in the 
same line of work as me,

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:09.740
so I took on his identity and 
covered the whole thing up.

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:12.900
It was like he never died.

00:16:12.900 --> 00:16:15.110
I'm impressed that no one found out.

00:16:15.110 --> 00:16:17.060
My superior was my big brother, see.

00:16:17.060 --> 00:16:19.020
He managed to hush it up.

00:16:19.020 --> 00:16:21.470
Hush it up? How?

00:16:21.470 --> 00:16:26.330
When he came to relieve me, 
he brought a spare life with him.

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:30.130
<i>That's a common urban 
legend in our business.</i>

00:16:30.570 --> 00:16:31.750
<i>Which means...</i>

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:36.350
<i>Is he a member of that silver race, 
the Intergalactic Defense Force?!</i>

00:16:37.400 --> 00:16:40.860
He was my masterpiece!

00:16:41.470 --> 00:16:44.320
No one could have beaten him.

00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:47.730
He was my first, my greatest creation!

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:51.360
The entire world would have 
been in our hands by now.

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:56.580
For creating him, I should have been lauded, 
promoted to the ranks of the elite!

00:16:56.580 --> 00:17:01.610
But it all went up in smoke... 
just because of one little mistake.

00:17:01.610 --> 00:17:03.360
That story again?

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:06.130
You should really get over it. 
It's all in the past.

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:11.140
I gave him the ultimate body, 
the ultimate combat prowess.

00:17:11.140 --> 00:17:14.270
And yet... because he got away 
before I altered his brain,

00:17:14.270 --> 00:17:15.580
we ended up having to fight him!

00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:18.880
Why did you do it, my terrifying
 monster, Grasshopper Man?!

00:17:18.880 --> 00:17:21.340
<i>Nowadays, we always create 
a monster's loyal brain first</i>

00:17:21.340 --> 00:17:24.160
<i>so they won't just run off with 
the combat prowess we gave them.</i>

00:17:24.160 --> 00:17:28.170
<i>The incident he's describing 
is famous in our industry,</i>

00:17:28.170 --> 00:17:30.900
<i>and the reason we adopted the practice.</i>

00:17:30.900 --> 00:17:33.690
If only I'd altered his brain first!

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:35.120
But because of that one tiny mistake,

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:38.910
every future iteration of our 
organization has been destroyed.

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:44.300
<i>Is he one of the white combatants from 
that renowned legacy secret society?</i>

00:17:44.680 --> 00:17:45.910
Does that mean...

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:47.950
You use a car, you're a driver.

00:17:47.950 --> 00:17:49.790
You use a train, you're an engineer.

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:51.710
If you're not on a motorcycle, 
how the hell are you a Ri—

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:54.590
I hear his boss is so strict, he can't even 
transform without the guy's permission.

00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:57.210
Overloading the miniaturized 
nuclear reactor in your legs

00:17:57.210 --> 00:18:00.810
to kick a guy with fire doesn't 
quite seem fair, does it?

00:18:00.810 --> 00:18:04.860
<i>Is this a watering hole for retired 
heroes and evil organization staff?!</i>

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:09.320
<i>This is bad... I can't let 
them realize who I really am!</i>

00:18:09.320 --> 00:18:11.800
Are you in the business, miss?

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:14.200
What? Oh, well...

00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:17.090
It's all right. I can tell.

00:18:17.090 --> 00:18:18.070
It's in your eyes.

00:18:18.340 --> 00:18:21.020
You want to hear something ridiculous?

00:18:21.020 --> 00:18:24.940
Let me tell you, girlie, about this 
devious little gang I used to fight!

00:18:24.940 --> 00:18:26.580
Y-Yes?

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:29.630
I'd send out one of my little ones, 
just doing his best all on his own,

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:32.970
and they'd gang up on him, five-on-one!

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:35.980
Pulling out their whatever-you-call-it 
combination moves...

00:18:35.980 --> 00:18:38.350
Five people dogpiling one sweet little guy!

00:18:38.350 --> 00:18:40.890
Can you believe the cruelty?

00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:45.150
And if I sent out a big one, 
they'd call in the stinking robot!

00:18:45.150 --> 00:18:46.880
My boy's out there with just his fists,

00:18:46.880 --> 00:18:49.070
and they're busting out the heavy machinery!

00:18:49.070 --> 00:18:53.000
Not even the world's greatest martial 
artists can beat a bulldozer, you know?

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:55.470
Totally unfair, right?

00:18:56.110 --> 00:19:00.120
I knew she wanted me to do it.

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:02.150
Wow, you were a ladies' man!

00:19:02.150 --> 00:19:04.110
She was beautiful.

00:19:04.110 --> 00:19:05.460
And of course, I was a man.

00:19:05.460 --> 00:19:07.910
There was plenty I wanted 
to do with her, too.

00:19:07.910 --> 00:19:10.590
Again and again and again...

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:14.280
But I never had the guts.

00:19:14.280 --> 00:19:16.030
Hey, it happens.

00:19:16.030 --> 00:19:17.480
You were just a kid, right?

00:19:17.480 --> 00:19:19.620
Yes, I was so young then.

00:19:19.890 --> 00:19:23.110
But do you realize the 
conflict I went through?

00:19:23.110 --> 00:19:28.120
Every time I tried to take off her blouse, 
I got so afraid, my hands just froze...

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:30.030
Because... Because...

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:35.150
The third button down was 
the detonator for a bomb!

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:39.640
I guess it would feel about that 
dangerous to a young guy, huh?

00:19:39.850 --> 00:19:42.910
N-No, I don't mean that. I mean 
she had a bomb in her chest...

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:45.170
Dynamite sexy, right?

00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:49.400
Say that again! I dare you!

00:19:50.420 --> 00:19:52.250
I'll say it as many times it takes!

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:56.430
Bozos like you people can 
never conquer the world!

00:19:56.430 --> 00:19:59.540
I object to being grouped in with them.

00:19:59.540 --> 00:20:01.170
You damned fool!

00:20:01.910 --> 00:20:04.750
Tagenji! Daichiman!

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:10.170
I don't wanna hear big talk from someone 
who loses to that fatso Daichiman!

00:20:10.430 --> 00:20:12.690
You have no right to lecture me.

00:20:13.090 --> 00:20:15.900
Bandou Bujin Musashi has arrived!

00:20:16.330 --> 00:20:19.730
Musashi beats you every time, loser!

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:22.450
I'd rather be a loser...

00:20:23.230 --> 00:20:25.340
Slider Kamen Ryukishi!

00:20:25.340 --> 00:20:31.450
...than a dumbass who gets his own suit 
stolen by his rival Dragon Knight.

00:20:31.450 --> 00:20:33.210
I'll kill you, asshole!

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:34.960
And what about you?

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:37.460
My only wish is for smiles of joy!

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:39.610
Koshu Kid, Tryon!

00:20:39.610 --> 00:20:44.210
You're just a bunch of old men who 
can't beat Tryon in a five-on-one!

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:49.460
None of you will leave this shop alive!

00:20:49.460 --> 00:20:51.230
I'll see that you regret that threat!

00:20:51.440 --> 00:20:53.720
Be quiet and listen, pathetic swine.

00:20:53.720 --> 00:20:56.730
I'll slice you all to pieces right here!

00:20:56.730 --> 00:20:57.830
This is awful!

00:20:59.560 --> 00:21:01.880
Oh, are they at it again?

00:21:02.680 --> 00:21:05.360
It's good to see the young folk in the 
business still have so much energy.

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:06.990
It's not good at all!

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:08.700
Look at those fools!

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:11.970
Pipiruma Panpuru!

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:13.820
Kurukuru Rinkuru!

00:21:13.820 --> 00:21:17.250
Mahariku Tekumaku Furuuru Sharanra!

00:21:17.440 --> 00:21:19.010
With just one fancy touch...

00:21:19.200 --> 00:21:22.120
a beautiful debut!

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:28.830
Magical Punishment!

00:21:36.810 --> 00:21:40.170
If you jerks wanna fight, take it outside!

00:21:40.810 --> 00:21:42.820
We're sorry, ma'am!

00:21:45.390 --> 00:21:48.310
You're a former magical girl, ma'am?

00:21:49.850 --> 00:21:52.750
<i>Retirement is equally hard on good and evil.</i>

00:21:52.750 --> 00:21:54.830
<i>Neither job comes with transferable skills.</i>

